      "writtenOn": "2019-04-11T04:49:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is getting the proxy value per FS configuration, which means the proxy must be configured on each FS, i.e.:\n\n [fs \"foo\"]\n     proxy \u003d /path/to/proxy\n [fs \"bar\"]\n     proxy \u003d /path/to/proxy\n\nand if it\u0027s not configured on one of them, that one will fall back to the canonical URL.\n\nWouldn\u0027t it be better to make this a config that\u0027s effective for all FS backends? I.e.\n\n [fs]\n     proxy \u003d /path/to/proxy\n\nand then the setting should be read without passing the backend name, i.e.:\n\n  String proxy \u003d config.getString(backend.type.name(), null, PROXY);",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "b7da47f6fdbd03f52731e2f2b3705a05e121614d",
